.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt WGET 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm wget
.Nd simple HTTP and verified HTTPS download
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl q
.Op Fl O Ar file
.Op Fl -max-time Ar seconds
.Op Fl -cacert Ar file
.Ar URL
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility performs one bounded HTTP GET and saves the response body to
.Ar file
when
.Fl O
is present, otherwise to the last path segment of
.Ar URL .
An empty path or a trailing slash becomes
.Pa index.html .
The names
.Sq \&.
and
.Sq \&..
are rejected.
An existing file is overwritten.
.Pp
The base build is plain HTTP and does not link C or OpenSSL; an
.Pa https://
URL fails with a clear
.Dv EUNAVAILABLE
message.
The optional TLS add-on build links
.Xr raven-tls 3
and the owner-approved OpenSSL add-on and verifies the certificate chain and
the host name or IP address.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl O Ar file
Write to
.Ar file .
The value
.Sq -
means standard output.
.It Fl q
Suppress the summary and diagnostics.
.It Fl -max-time Ar seconds
Set the total request deadline in seconds.
The default is 10.
.It Fl -cacert Ar file
TLS add-on build only: trust exactly this PEM bundle instead of the default
.Pa /addons/etc/ssl/certs/ca-bundle.pem .
.El
.Pp
Redirects are followed with a bounded budget.
There is no recursive spidering, resume, POST, cookie jar or shell execution.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr curl 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
This is a deliberately small subset, not a GNU wget replacement.
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in RavenBSD 0.1.0.
